================================================================================
3.0  STANDARDS OF PROFESSIONAL CONDUCT
================================================================================

3.1  UNIVERSAL RESPECT
     We do not use protected categories. We enforce a Universal Standard.

     > HARASSMENT-FREE
       No offensive verbal comments, intimidation, or stalking. The goal is a 
       neutral environment for deep work.

     > CIVIL DISCOURSE
       Attack problems, not people. Dissent must be professional (e.g., in 
       code reviews) and devoid of personal insult.

3.2  TECHNICAL HUMILITY
     > NO "TECH-SHAMING"
       We do not belittle choice of IDE, OS, or style.

     > NO FEIGNING SURPRISE
       Disbelief (e.g., "I can't believe you don't know USSD") is banned. 
       It destroys psychological safety.

     > NO "WELL-ACTUALLY'S"
       Pedantic corrections that do not improve the outcome are discouraged.

================================================================================
4.0  TECHNICAL INTEGRITY
================================================================================

4.1  SANDBOX STEWARDSHIP
     > LOAD TESTING
       High-volume testing in the shared Sandbox without auth is Disruptive 
       Behavior (DoS).

     > LOOP PREVENTION
       Developers must ensure logic does not create infinite loops that drain 
       resources.

4.2  SECURITY
     > THE "NO-KEYS" RULE
       Posting raw API keys/secrets in public channels is a security incident. 
       Moderators will delete immediately.

     > IMPERSONATION
       Configuring Sender IDs to impersonate AT staff, Gov bodies, or Banks 
       is a severe violation.

4.3  OPEN SOURCE
     > PERMISSION & LIABILITY
       Code is shared "as is" (MIT License ethos). Users implement advice at 
       their own risk.

     > ATTRIBUTION
       Plagiarism of code or tutorials is prohibited.

================================================================================
5.0  COMPLIANCE & GOVERNANCE
================================================================================

5.1  CONTENT SAFETY (SHAFT)
     Applies to SMS, USSD, Voice, Chat. Compliance is binary.

     > PROHIBITED (SHAFT)
       Sex, Hate, Alcohol, Firearms, Tobacco.

     > CHAT SPECIFICS
       Distribution of illicit/violent imagery via Chat API is banned.

5.2  VALUE TRANSFER (AIRTIME/DATA)
     > AML PROTOCOLS
       Discussions on converting (washing) Airtime/Data to cash to bypass 
       banking regs are banned.

     > FRAUD
       Solicitation to exploit billing bugs or bypass KYC is grounds for 
       immediate expulsion.

5.3  DATA PRIVACY
     > PII PROTECTION
       Sharing real phone numbers for "testing" is banned. Use dummy data.

     > CONSENT
       Building "scrapers" to harvest numbers without consent is prohibited.

================================================================================
6.0  EVENT PROTOCOLS (PHYSICAL/VIRTUAL)
================================================================================

6.1  HACKATHONS
     > INTELLECTUAL HONESTY
       Submitting pre-existing work as new ("sandbagging") is prohibited.

     > VENUE RESPECT
       Vandalism or misuse of hub/university equipment = Expulsion.

6.2  VIRTUAL SPACES
     > SPAM
       Unsolicited DMs selling services/recruiting are banned.

     > BOTS
       Bots must provide value and have a "kill switch."

